{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation","id":1547193,"title":"Sahar-Hannibaal Generation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-22T22:27:59-08:00","id":1547193,"title":"Sahar-Hannibaal Generation","content":"As some of you might be aware of, Sahar-Hannibaal is the leader of the Moloch faction within the clan Baali. He's a notorious cainite and has been covered in some books. One thing that I find confusing is his generation in his published character's sheet in the Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, where he's listed as being of the 7th generation, yet has quite a few traits at level 8. In your opinion is his generation a typo or is he one of those characters who have traits above their generation limit (like 2nd edition Valerius Maior, for instance, another one listed as 7th generation who had level 8 traits, his v20 character sheet changes it, though)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T02:20:27-08:00","id":1547194,"title":"","content":"In his case, Daimonion provides an explanation for the boosted attributes, especially if you assume he uses the Dark Ages version of Daimonion 6 (in V20 it's an infernal pact, in DA it's an Investiture which better fits the Order of Moloch). He also has Dur-An-Ki to fall back on.<br /> <br /> In general I tend to brush over discrepancies like this, since there are many ways around the generational limit for PCs, and for low gen NPCs it makes sense that they would make use of the same exploits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T02:24:18-08:00","id":1547195,"title":"","content":"He is among the few we know his line thanks to Clanbook: Baali, Dark Ages Europe, Road of Sin, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra<br /> <b>Sahar-Hannibaal</b>, childe of <b>Tanitbaal-Sahar</b>\u200b, child of <b>Tanit</b>\u200b, child of <b>Moloch, </b>child of lets say Saulot<br /> He is 7th Generation like Safirah, Tanitbaal-Sahar's other children from DA V20\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T08:37:47-08:00","id":1547200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547194#post1547194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In his case, Daimonion provides an explanation for the boosted attributes, especially if you assume he uses the Dark Ages version of Daimonion 6 (in V20 it's an infernal pact, in DA it's an Investiture which better fits the Order of Moloch). He also has Dur-An-Ki to fall back on.<br /> <br /> In general I tend to brush over discrepancies like this, since there are many ways around the generational limit for PCs, and for low gen NPCs it makes sense that they would make use of the same exploits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like the idea of giving possibilities of characters having traits above the generational limit, still the thing about Hannibaal is that he has a lot of traits at 8 or 7, including disciplines, so, for instance, most ST I know would prefer to go the &quot;normal path&quot; of considering his generation a mistake (WW has made quite a few of these confusing things like characters with traits above their generational limit and in many cases the generation wasn't really clear). I'm asking more to know if you're as STs like the idea of allowing characters to have traits above their &quot;expected limits&quot; through different means, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He is among the few we know his line thanks to Clanbook: Baali, Dark Ages Europe, Road of Sin, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra<br /> <b>Sahar-Hannibaal</b>, childe of <b>Tanitbaal-Sahar</b>, child of <b>Tanit</b>\u200b, child of <b>Moloch, </b>child of lets say Saulot<br /> He is 7th Generation like Safirah, Tanitbaal-Sahar's other children from DA V20\u200b\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>Yes, indeed he's one of the few we know his line, but still he could have commited diablerie. As I said above, I know there are different kinds of STs, ons who prefer to go &quot;stricktly by the rules&quot; and others who are more lenient in regards to generational limit, etc. So in which group are you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T14:57:17-08:00","id":1547207,"title":"","content":"Another explanation is that, being the founder of the Road of Sin, he might have reached some kind of alternative Golconda that removes the trait limit regardless of generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T16:27:00-08:00","id":1547208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation#post1547193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your opinion is his generation a typo or is he one of those characters who have traits above their generation limit (like 2nd edition Valerius Maior, for instance, another one listed as 7th generation who had level 8 traits, his v20 character sheet changes it, though)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Valerius Maior's extra power the result of him being possessed by the spirit of an infernal sorcerer from the Roman Empire? There was a lot of early weirdness/special snowflake syndrome around the character.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T20:16:55-08:00","id":1547211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547207#post1547207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another explanation is that, being the founder of the Road of Sin, he might have reached some kind of alternative Golconda that removes the trait limit regardless of generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's his sire, Tanitbaal-Sahar. Sahar-Hannibaal reformed the Road of the Hive and later had an epiphany of sorts turning him Bahari which might go in the same direction, though. I also get the two mixed up constantly due to the lineage naming scheme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547200#post1547200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm asking more to know if you're as STs like the idea of allowing characters to have traits above their &quot;expected limits&quot; through different means, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer some extra stats over changing generation for canon NPCs, but just because it means less effort to keep track of lineages. Changing the generation is more likely to cause inconsistencies than a few dots, especially for characters that have a somewhat defined lineage. Homebrew NPCs usually stay within generational limits though - if I really, really need them to have access to Power X that would be outside of their scope, some artifact or pact does the trick. Or custom blood-sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T02:19:19-08:00","id":1547212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's his sire, Tanitbaal-Sahar. Sahar-Hannibaal reformed the Road of the Hive and later had an epiphany of sorts turning him Bahari which might go in the same direction, though. I also get the two mixed up constantly due to the lineage naming scheme. </div> </div> </div>True, I also sometimes used to get them mixed up. In fact Sahar-Hannibaal had this &quot;strange sort of epiphany&quot;, still in his character's sheet he has a 9 in his Road of the Hive rating, which, along with other things makes me consider where exactly is his faith supposed to be according to the official lore.In any case, giving his level 9 Road rating I wouldn't see a problem and in fact would consider interesting if a ST used this &quot;sort of Golconda&quot; to justify his traits. The Road of the Hive is a particularly interesting Road in my opinion, I ned to add.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I prefer some extra stats over changing generation for canon NPCs, but just because it means less effort to keep track of lineages. Changing the generation is more likely to cause inconsistencies than a few dots, especially for characters that have a somewhat defined lineage. Homebrew NPCs usually stay within generational limits though - if I really, really need them to have access to Power X that would be outside of their scope, some artifact or pact does the trick. Or custom blood-sorcery. </div> </div> </div>Yes, to be honest, where it might cause trouble, I also prefer to go this way. Still, I'm normally not opposed to the idea of allowing characters (NPCs or PCs) to have the possibility of geetting stats above their generation limit, through &quot;mysterious ways&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wasn't Valerius Maior's extra power the result of him being possessed by the spirit of an infernal sorcerer from the Roman Empire? There was a lot of early weirdness/special snowflake syndrome around the character. </div> </div> </div>Yes, in his case, Varro offers a good argument for his higher traits (even though, his new/revised sheet in V20 Dread Names, got rid of all of this IIRC), but let's not forget that this sort of thing has happened many times in WWs history and often it's solved by fixing the generation, like with Lucius Trebius Rufus, who in Jerusalem by Night had his generation as 10th, yet had many traits above his generational limit (most notably Dominate 7, but also Presence 6).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T04:17:45-08:00","id":1547215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547212#post1547212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, I also sometimes used to get them mixed up. In fact Sahar-Hannibaal had this &quot;strange sort of epiphany&quot;, still in his character's sheet he has a 9 in his Road of the Hive rating, which, along with other things makes me consider where exactly is his faith supposed to be according to the official lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one thing that bugged me a bit about his story. He has this grand vision after casting an ancient spell and the result is a Thaumaturgy Path that ties the Children of Lilith and the Baali Children of the Outer Dark together. Which is fine as a concept (although it really should either have been Dur-An-Ki or a Daimonion variant), but one would think he would incorporate this revelation more into his personal morality and the Order of Moloch. Meaning, another revision of the Path of the Hive.<br /> If I run him in one of my Chronicles again, I would give him the Road of the Hive/Road of Lilith <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535897#post1535897\">crossover</a> I made for Lamiae Apostates.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T08:30:59-08:00","id":1547220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547215#post1547215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one thing that bugged me a bit about his story. He has this grand vision after casting an ancient spell and the result is a Thaumaturgy Path that ties the Children of Lilith and the Baali Children of the Outer Dark together. Which is fine as a concept (although it really should either have been Dur-An-Ki or a Daimonion variant), but one would think he would incorporate this revelation more into his personal morality and the Order of Moloch. Meaning, another revision of the Path of the Hive.<br /> If I run him in one of my Chronicles again, I would give him the Road of the Hive/Road of Lilith <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1535897#post1535897\">crossover</a> I made for Lamiae Apostates.</div> </div> </div> </div>The path you created is really interesting I feel the need to mention. In fact, I liked the vision you had. It's also very interesting that it uses self-control, instead of Instincts (the virtue favored by the &quot;Abel's Angels&quot;). In fact as much as I like the Path of the Hive, it still feels a hard path to follow and many players argue about some of its teachings, the most problematic one is probably the very idea of &quot;causing havoc and destruction to keep the Sleepers from awakening&quot;. I've seen the discussion of how to justify some things, for instance, making a &quot;grand sacrifice&quot; resulting in many mortal deaths could be seen as &quot;causing havoc and destruction&quot;, but still the path is against even simpler things like feeding on mortals, etc. which, according to one of the players I once had makes one think that the path wants its followers to protect humans, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 12-24-2024, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T19:22:00-08:00","id":1547230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547200#post1547200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also like the idea of giving possibilities of characters having traits above the generational limit, still the thing about Hannibaal is that he has a lot of traits at 8 or 7, including disciplines, so, for instance, most ST I know would prefer to go the &quot;normal path&quot; of considering his generation a mistake (WW has made quite a few of these confusing things like characters with traits above their generational limit and in many cases the generation wasn't really clear). I'm asking more to know if you're as STs like the idea of allowing characters to have traits above their &quot;expected limits&quot; through different means, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bigger question is - are any of his powers 6+ <i><b>described</b></i>? Because otherwise i would qualify it as all too typical &quot;signature/pet NPC dot fat&quot;.<br /> <br /> And axe it all down everything to 6s, because if a writer can't be bothered to <i><b>define </b></i>its snowflake NPC supposed awesomeness, why should i take the effort to make it shine for the lazy hacks?<br /> <br /> Elder powers are <b><i>supposed </i></b>to be room for individuality AND customization - if <i>nothing </i>is described of <i>the baked in plot devices</i>, then <i><b>any </b></i>elder power will do, so 6s are fine and case closed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T08:17:38-08:00","id":1547260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547230#post1547230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bigger question is - are any of his powers 6+ <i><b>described</b></i>? Because otherwise i would qualify it as all too typical &quot;signature/pet NPC dot fat&quot;.<br /> <br /> And axe it all down everything to 6s, because if a writer can't be bothered to <i><b>define </b></i>its snowflake NPC supposed awesomeness, why should i take the effort to make it shine for the lazy hacks?<br /> <br /> Elder powers are <b><i>supposed </i></b>to be room for individuality AND customization - if <i>nothing </i>is described of <i>the baked in plot devices</i>, then <i><b>any </b></i>elder power will do, so 6s are fine and case closed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, very often we don't find any of a given character's powers 6+ described, I don't find it all that problmatic tbh. To cite an example, I don't remember a single character in Children of the Revolution with their 6+ powers describd, then again this is in my opinion one of those books where it seems they invited people with no idea about how to ST a game or give stats to a character, because I was appalled at how terribly written were the characters sheets in that book, it's as if I asked my grandma to give numbers to the characters I wrote about lol (meaning someone who has no clue what those numbers mean). Yes, it's that bad, it's even hard to pick one, there's this Apacia, a cainite of the Cappadocian clan who is old as sin and not only has a more ancillae level character sheet, but also doesn't have a way to become a snake that her story says she transforms herself into. Just to give a rather comical example. Sahar-Hannibaal at least has a character sheet that we can respect (even if it's perhaps not powerful enough, for &quot;the leader of the order of Moloch&quot;). Oh and I forgot to mention that according to her story, Apacia with her puny traits was able to: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although she was not Japheth\u2019s equal in age or potency of the blood, she was a dedicated warrior where he was not, and she broke him against the marble walls of the temple... </div> </div> </div> HAhaha, man one cainite doesn't really neeed to be &quot;a dedicated warrior&quot; to beat her ass, in a real world (or game) he could literally destroy her with a glance...sorry for the rant, but I was so disappointed with this book that well, I needed to rant a bit....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T12:22:34-08:00","id":1547281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547260#post1547260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, to be fair, very often we don't find any of a given character's powers 6+ described, I don't find it all that problmatic tbh.To cite an example, I don't remember a single character in Children of the Revolution with their 6+ powers describd, then again this is in my opinion one of those books where it seems they invited people with no idea about how to ST a game or give stats to a character, because I was appalled at how terribly written were the characters sheets in that book, it's as if I asked my grandma to give numbers to the characters I wrote about lol (meaning someone who has no clue what those numbers mean).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the writers started doing so with 1ed a World of Darkness and the notes on individual elder powers gradually disappeared, DC by Night with the notes on Vitel's powers (that <i><b>could not be left out</b></i> since him having the right set of elder powers is a major part of the book's plot, might be said) is probably the last to do so. But becoming the norm doesn't mean it's a good thing or acceptable.<br /> <br /> And the big irony is that this behaviour we have come to tolerate - in your own words, you don't find it all that problmatic tbh - <b><i>is directly at the root</i></b> of the sketchy NPC stats you railed about right after. It's at least a major symptom/telltale sign of a common problem of writers unsure of how to insert their ideas into the mechanics (or just throwing numbers with little to no care for consistency) behind both.<br /> <br /> (There's probably also some snowflake love/hate issues not to mention runaway budding novelist syndrome mixed in at least a few cases but i digress - and probably edging too close to personally offending people i barely know and probably left for other business ages ago - so let me close the rant and focus on other things)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547260#post1547260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's that bad, it's even hard to pick one, there's this Apacia, a cainite of the Cappadocian clan who is old as sin and not only has a more ancillae level character sheet, but also doesn't have a way to become a snake that her story says she transforms herself into. Just to give a rather comical example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to admit that i've never read Children of the Revolution though i do have the pdf, so i had to do a quick wiki search to even know who the hell that is supposed to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And surprisingly, i didn't find her half as bad as you seemed to indicate. Bear with me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Apparently she was embraced sometime in the 500s BCE, what would make her about 2500 years, potentially an equal of Dastur Anosh <b>and </b>give her up to 50 dots in disciplines, if using the guidelines in Children of the Night (that i do find quite helpful in keeping things consistent). Potentially, <b><i>if </i></b>she had been awake and active for all of that time - what from just a quick look into her story is definitely <b>not </b>the case, as she seems to have gone through centuries-long torpor periods at least three times in her existence.<br /> <br /> I <i>think </i>that all put together they might amount to 1000 years, meaning Apacia is closer to 1500 years of active unlife, meaning that she would more probably be in the 35-40 dots ballpark.<br /> Her sheet in the wiki gives about 32 dots (not counting 18 dots in necromantic paths), so, below the mark but not awfuly so, for a character in the blurry line between top tier elder and meth it kind of fits. Definitely <b>not </b>ancilla-level.<br /> <br /> And one more thing - her story does <b>not </b>say she transforms herself into a snake, it's more like &quot;<i>Vykos infected her with something (</i>oh, joy....<i>) during their vaulderie rites/fling</i>&quot; and it manifests as changing tattoos and some serpentine cosmetic features to her appearance, specially when working her blood magic. It's basically a funky easter egg of latent but undeveloped vicissitude - maybe even some weird connection to the Dracon (that was still inside Vykos back in the 1800s when they met).<br /> <br /> As an aside, i'll admit i probably have a soft spot for her due to how much she reminds me of Magog, a friend's PC from &quot;a methuselah game&quot; we were part of (more than) a few years back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547260#post1547260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and I forgot to mention that according to her story, Apacia with her puny traits was able to:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Although she was not Japheth\u2019s equal in age or potency of the blood, she was a dedicated warrior where he was not, and she broke him against the marble walls of the temple</b>...</i><br /> <br /> Hahaha, man one cainite doesn't really neeed to be &quot;a dedicated warrior&quot; to beat her ass, in a real world (or game) he could literally destroy her with a glance...sorry for the rant, but I was so disappointed with this book that well, I needed to rant a bit....</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw the thing, in the wiki at least. She has 5, 7, 7 on physicals, most combat skills on 6 (weirdly no archery or throwing, that should be musts for an unliving warrior goddess of an elder) and Celerity 4, Fortitude 6, Potence 5, Courage 5, Willpower 8, making the idea of her pouncing on Japheth and ramming him into the walls of the Erciyes thanks to frenzy <i>and sheer shock of a clanmate daring to do so</i> to Japheth <b>almost </b>believable. It was no grudge match or battle among near-equals, it was the angry school kid whose punch from nowhere stunned the teacher (but yeah, all 6-7s in those disciplines would have made things much more convincing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547193-sahar-hannibaal-generation?p=1547260#post1547260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sahar-Hannibaal at least has a character sheet that we can respect (even if it's perhaps not powerful enough, for &quot;the leader of the order of Moloch&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;True Hand&quot; is just another Gehenna cult but with better networking and some weird tricks on their sleeves, i think you overestimate the actual capacities of the Tal'Mahe'Ra due to hype and snowflake. Daimoinon &amp; Thaumaturgy 7 are definitely NOT something for people to sneeze at, at all.<br /> <br /> Not to mention he is the <i>current </i>leader of the order of Moloch, as he has been since the 1190s-1200s, when Tanit fell to torpor due to Azaneal's shenanigans.<br /> There's nothing to stop Tanit or some other less known heavy-hitter among the Molochites Baali from &quot;pulling an Ur-Shulgi&quot; so to speak on the order and turning things completely on its head. Older or younger, coming up with potential rivals or prospective sucessors to Sahar-Hannibaal could provide plenty of fodder for chronicles where the True Hand figure proeminently.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-27-2024, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T23:47:54-08:00","id":1547293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And surprisingly, i didn't find her half as bad as you seemed to indicate. Bear with me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that she's not really terribly designed, I just found that the whole book has some characters whose influence in the setting is supposed to be huge, but most of their character's sheets are subpar, ofc I exaggerated in saying that Apacia is &quot;ancillae level&quot;, but for someone supposed to be so awesome, her traits falls short. The same could be said about many character's in the book, many whom are part of the <i>Manus Nigrum/Tal'Mahe'Ra</i>. Dastur Anosh, for being such a legendary figure has somewhat subpar traits, the same could be said about Roderigo al-Dakhil, etc. As you said <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>almost </b>believable\u200b </div> </div> </div> I mean, literaly Japheth could beat her up with his bare hands without much effort by the traits she was given.<br /> <br /> I've been Storytelling for more than 2 decades and half and I doubt many people have worked as a ST as much as I have through these years, there were years when I would ST everyday, my stories stretch years in real life and often centuries in game. I would often tell my friends who were starting, to understand that the traits you give a character is a very important aspect of said character, even more so when the players come in contact with said traits. It's safer to go with &quot;too much&quot; than with &quot;too little&quot;, players tend to ridicule characters whose traits do not match their supposed role. It reminds me of the old adage, like the ST who got saddened because the group somehow destroyed the cool character he created for the story, just because he cannot make a good character sheet, ofc the said stories happen more often with D&amp;D, but also in the WoD. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;True Hand&quot; is just another Gehenna cult but with better networking and some weird tricks on their sleeves, i think you overestimate the actual capacities of the Tal'Mahe'Ra due to hype and snowflake. </div> </div> </div>I definitelly don't overestimate their actual capacities &quot;due to hype and snowflake&quot; (especially because I'm definitely not a &quot;newcomer&quot; who is so naive as to be &quot;influenced&quot; by hype or whatever), they are not merely &quot;just another Gehenna cult&quot; they're THE gehenna cult (and it doesn't matter much the fact that the setting sometimes seemed to pretend they didn't exist, because of how polemic they were, etc), the thing is if the ST accepts them as being what they're supposed to be, they're basically the most powerful Sect in the setting.<br /> <br /> The main problem with Sahar-Hannibaal traits is that he lacks a real &quot;oomph&quot;, he could be made a bit more powerful, the fact that they didn't describe ANY of his advanced discipline powers as you pointed out, certainly doesn't help. Of course the fact that he has Blood Sorcery (Dur-an-Ki) 7 means that the ST could always have a card up his sleeve to use when needed, but it would be cooler if he had more &quot;offensive capabilities&quot; stated in his character's sheet. <br /> <br /> All in all, as has often being cite here in the forums, sometimes it seems they used to hire writers with no real knowledge of the game to give character's traits, in this case, it would be better to leave the characters unstatted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}